# Copy to .env (untracked, gitignored) to move any of these off their defaults.
# An exported shell variable wins over this file, and this file wins over the
# defaults in scripts/env.sh.
#
# Values are LITERAL - no ~ expansion, and only the keys listed in scripts/env.sh
# are read. Write absolute paths, or a path relative to E2631_WORK: a relative
# value resolves against that directory both in the shell helpers and in
# host/release.mjs, which is what makes one file usable from Linux and Windows.

# Where the build outputs go. $E2631_WORK/out is what docs/ mean by "out/".
E2631_WORK=/home/you/e2631-work

# The build tree: a depth-1 checkout of the tree fork's branch at the pinned
# commit (scripts/bootstrap.sh creates it, feeds included). T-12 retired the
# overlay/patch-series layout - device support now lives in the fork as real
# commits, so there is exactly one kind of tree.
E2631_TREE=/home/you/openwrt

# Advanced: point bootstrap at another fork/branch/depth. Leave these unset in
# normal use. E2631_FORK_SHA is NOT a .env key on purpose - the pin belongs to
# scripts/pins.env, and an override here is how a look-alike build gets made.
# The hooks exist so a local rehearsal can clone a path instead of GitHub.
#E2631_FORK_REPO=https://github.com/QC3284/immortalwrt
#E2631_FORK_BRANCH=e2631
#E2631_FORK_DEPTH=32

# Optional: reproduce the released v1.10.0 byte-for-byte (parity evidence P1/P4).
# bootstrap then writes version=r0-bde1448 and version.date=1794624080 into the
# tree topdir (untracked files) and the packer should be given the same build
# stamp, E2631_BUILD=20261114. Leave unset for ordinary builds.
#E2631_REPRODUCE_V1100=true
#E2631_BUILD=20261114

# Optional: the version-header template. Leave this unset and packing uses
# seed/vendor-verhdr-8b8.bin, the 532-byte header slice that ships with the repo -
# that is all `pack` reads out of a template. Set it to a full official ZTE upgrade
# package (relative form: <E2631_WORK>/vendor/...) only for mkfactory selftest/info,
# or to re-verify the shipped slice against vendor bytes you own.
#E2631_TEMPLATE=vendor/zxhn-e2631-official.bin

# Optional: stamp the project version into the 32-byte version field of the vendor
# header, so the LuCI slot table tells our slot from the stock one (the template
# carries the vendor's own "V1.0.0.8B8.8000" - without this both slots read
# identically). ASCII only, 31 bytes max. The 16-byte build field is always
# stamped: E2631_BUILD, else the pack date (YYYYMMDD).
#E2631_VERSION=ImmortalWrt v1.10.0
#E2631_BUILD=20261025

# Optional HTTP(S) proxy for the download phases. Leave it unset on a box with a
# working direct route.
#E2631_PROXY=http://192.168.1.10:7897
